course: dictionary
lesson: 1129
title: Breaststroke
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Breaststroke is a way of swimming on your front. Your arms push forward together and then sweep round to the sides, while your legs kick like a frog.
explain: «The four swimming strokes are front crawl, backstroke, breaststroke and butterfly.» The list tells you breaststroke is one of the four main strokes. Context clue: a name that sits in a list of things of the same kind.
explain: «In front crawl the arms do most of the pushing, and the legs kick mainly to keep the body flat.» Compare the two: in breaststroke the arms and legs both push, with the arms moving together. When you are not sure, swap in your meaning, "swimming on your front with a frog kick", and check it still makes sense.
fact: Breaststroke is a way of swimming on your front.
fact: In breaststroke your arms push forward together and sweep round to the sides, while your legs kick like a frog.
fact: A breaststroke is one stroke in this style, so "a breaststroke" means one single stroke.
fact: Breaststroke is the slowest of the four racing strokes.
fact: Useful phrases: swim breaststroke, breaststroke kick, frog kick, 100 metres breaststroke.
exercise: «The four swimming strokes are front crawl, backstroke, breaststroke and butterfly.» In this sentence, what is breaststroke? | A dance move | A kind of football kick | A type of fish | *A way of swimming, one of the four main strokes
exercise: In breaststroke, what do your legs do? | Stay completely still | Kick up high like a kangaroo | Flap up and down like a bird | *Kick like a frog
exercise: Which of these is the slowest of the four racing strokes? | *Breaststroke | Butterfly | Backstroke | Front crawl
test: In breaststroke, which way are you facing? | On your side | Upside down | *On your front | Up at the sky
test: Why do children often learn breaststroke early? | *Because you can keep your head up and see where you are going | Because it is the fastest stroke | Because you need no arms | Because it is only for adults
exam: Ella says a breaststroke kick is the same as a frog kick. Is she right? | No, a frog kick is a dance move | No, a frog kick is only used in butterfly | *Yes, the leg kick in breaststroke is like a frog kick | No, a frog kick is a swimming turn
